  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Pebrellin and the CD70 antigen, mediated through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This complex is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (2R,3R,4S,5R)-2-(6-aminopurin-9-yl)-5-methanidyl-tetrahydrofuran-3,4-diol and (4aR,7R,8aR)-4a-methyl-7-prop-1-en-2-yl-4,5,6,7,8,8a-hexahydro-3H-naphthalene-1-carboxylic acid, both of which have a final score of 0.54. These compounds are implicated in targeting the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn is associated with the CD70 antigen. The evidence indicates that Pebrellin may interact with this complex, potentially modulating the CD70 antigen's expression or function. The relationship is supported by multiple pathways, suggesting a possible role in regulatory mechanisms involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. However, the exact nature of the interaction and its functional implications remain to be fully elucidated."
